    {
     "type": "tip",
     "tag": "Language focus",
     "title": "Six little words for place",
     "steps": [
      [
       "in",
       "in the wardrobe · in the bag"
      ],
      [
       "on",
       "on the bunk · on the desk"
      ],
      [
       "under",
       "under the bunk"
      ],
      [
       "behind",
       "behind the door"
      ],
      [
       "next to",
       "next to the laundry"
      ],
      [
       "above",
       "above the desk"
      ]
     ],
     "paras": [
      "To say where something is: <b>It's</b> + place word + <b>the</b> + thing.",
      "<b>In</b> = inside. <b>On</b> = on top, touching. <b>Above</b> = higher, not touching."
     ],
     "avoid": "It's in under the bunk. · It's next the door. · It's on the wardrobe (if it's inside)."
    },
    {
     "type": "choice",
     "q": "The lifejacket is inside the wardrobe. It's ___ the wardrobe.",
     "opts": [
      "in",
      "on",
      "above"
     ],
     "a": 0
    },
    {
     "type": "choice",
     "q": "The muster card is on the back of the door. It's ___ the door.",
     "opts": [
      "behind",
      "under",
      "next"
     ],
     "a": 0
    },
    {
     "type": "choice",
     "q": "Which one is correct?",
     "opts": [
      "The stairs are next to the laundry.",
      "The stairs are next the laundry.",
      "The stairs are next of the laundry."
     ],
     "a": 0,
     "why": "Always next TO."
    },
    {
     "type": "build",
     "situation": "Tanya asks: \"Where's the immersion suit?\"",
     "q": "Answer her.",
     "a": [
      "It's",
      "under",
      "the",
      "bunk."
     ],
     "extra": [
      "in",
      "on"
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "tip",
     "tag": "Spanish speaker alert",
     "title": "\"En\" is not always \"in\"",
     "paras": [
      "In Spanish, <i>en</i> works for everything: <i>en el placard, en la cucheta, en la cubierta</i>. In English you choose: <b>in</b> the wardrobe (inside), <b>on</b> the bunk (on top), <b>on</b> the boat deck (a deck is a surface).",
      "<i>Arriba de</i> can be <b>on</b> (touching) or <b>above</b> (not touching)."
     ],
     "avoid": "in the bunk (if it's on top) · in the boat deck · on the wardrobe (if it's inside)"
    },
    {
     "type": "choice",
     "q": "My muster station is ___ the boat deck.",
     "opts": [
      "on",
      "in",
      "at the"
     ],
     "a": 0,
     "why": "A deck is a surface: ON the boat deck."
    },
    {
     "type": "choice",
     "q": "The porthole is higher than the desk, not touching it. It's ___ the desk.",
     "opts": [
      "above",
      "on",
      "in"
     ],
     "a": 0
    },
    {
     "type": "tip",
     "tag": "Pronunciation",
     "title": "Small words go fast",
     "paras": [
      "In <i>It's in the wardrobe</i>, the strong word is <b>WARDrobe</b>. <i>It's in the</i> is quick and soft: <i>itsinthe</i>.",
      "When you correct, the place word becomes strong: <i>Not ON the wardrobe. IN the wardrobe.</i>"
     ],
